9.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: Draw approximately **3.51 mL**.

The In-111 chloride vial is calibrated as **10 mCi in 10 mL = 1 mCi/mL** at Dec 26 12:00. Using the In-111 half-life of about **67.3 h**, the time from Dec 23 04:04 CST to Dec 26 12:00 is **79 h 56 min = 79.93 h**. Since the compounding time is before calibration, back-decay the concentration:

\[
C = 1\ \text{mCi/mL} \times 2^{79.93/67.3}
  = 1 \times 2^{1.1877}
  \approx 2.28\ \text{mCi/mL}
\]

Then:

\[
V = \frac{8\ \text{mCi}}{2.28\ \text{mCi/mL}}
  \approx 3.51\ \text{mL}
\]

So the volume to draw at 4:04 am is about **3.51 mL**.

